(Bug #95, the false rejection the same root cause produced. The name is
 declared on line 1 and read on line 2, which is the order LANGUAGE.md's
 "Declaration Order" asks for. The `Set` on line 3 is a later write, but the
 whole-program pre-pass counts an untyped `Set` as a declaration, so line 1
 was read as a reassignment of a name nothing had declared yet - and this
 program was rejected with "'tally' is used before it is declared".)

tally is 5.
Print tally.
Set tally to 7.
Print tally.

the label is "first".
Print label.
Set label to "second".
Print label.
